| `make fe-browsers` `[read]` | Downloads the browser each frontend app's journey drives into the runner's per-user cache, through the app's npm script `test:e2e:browsers`; with `install_sources.browser_download_host` set, it exports that mirror as `PLAYWRIGHT_DOWNLOAD_HOST` first, and null leaves the caller's own. | `make fe-browsers` | [`FE_APPS`](settings.md#make-variables), [`FE_BROWSER_FLAGS`](settings.md#make-variables), [`install_sources.browser_download_host`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`scripts/install_sources.py source`](settings.md#command-line-flags) | Reads the network and writes outside the tree, in the user's browser cache. Exits 0 with no output when no frontend app is found, and exits 2 like `make test-fe-unit` when `npm` or `node` is missing or an app lacks `node_modules/.package-lock.json`, npm's completion marker. Not for running the journey: `make test-fe-e2e`. | [limits-and-troubleshooting.md](../guides/limits-and-troubleshooting.md) | always |
